From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:59:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/34] coherent: a signal is seen once the writes before it
 are in the pages (E1)

A shared event's value, read from the semaphore's counter or seen at the
completion turn, rose before the turn armed the pages of the command buffers it
finished, so a guest that saw the value could read a trapping surface's held
pages with their older bytes (upstream review E1). Three paths, each a lane
that failed at 76ab0722:

- A signal after the writer's command buffer: a signal kept while a tracked
  surface holds open or running writes (shadow_coherent::unarmed, which waits
  for no lock) is behind the arm: no counter read observes it or any after it,
  and no wait is handed its index; the completion turn does. Ported by hand
  from upstream 76d89d87 (EventTimeline::keep's behind_merge, the observe_read
  clamp, landing), with its timeline unit test. Counted:
  CoherentFallbackCounts::signals_behind_arm.
- The completion turn arms the pages of each command buffer its batches end
  (shadow_lazy::completing) before their signals are seen; complete() finds
  them armed.
- A plain event's chain (writer signals an MTLEvent, a relay on another queue
  waits for it and signals a shared one): copy_back_before_signal now runs
  before every event signal, not only a shared event's.

Open, its lane ignored and run by name: a command buffer committed to wait for
a shared event draws over a surface the guest writes before setting it; the
encoder's copy in was decided as it was encoded (Coherent::taking), so the
draw misses the write. It needs a copy in recorded as the held batch goes.

Lanes (filter "surface", ANV): 129 passed 4 failed before (06:41Z), 131
passed 1 failed after (06:49Z); the failure is ycbcr_textures, as before.
Event lanes 24/24. Runtime unit tests 1149 -> 1150 passed, the one failure
(exit_guard) as at 76ab0722.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
